    <h2 id="how-to-reach">How to Reach Chittorgarh Fort</h2>
    <ul>
        <li><strong>By train:</strong> Chittorgarh Junction is well connected with Delhi, Jaipur, Ajmer, Udaipur, Kota, Indore and Mumbai. The fort is a short drive from the station.</li>
        <li><strong>By air:</strong> The nearest airport is Maharana Pratap Airport, Udaipur, about 90 km away. Read our <a href="Udaipur-Airport-to-Chittorgarh-Taxi.aspx">Udaipur Airport to Chittorgarh taxi guide</a>.</li>
        <li><strong>By road:</strong> Chittorgarh sits on major national highways linking it to Udaipur, Bhilwara, Ajmer, Jaipur and Kota. See our <a href="Chittorgarh-to-Udaipur-Taxi.aspx">Chittorgarh to Udaipur route guide</a>.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="taxi-tour">Exploring the Fort by Taxi</h2>
    <p>
        The fort plateau is huge &ndash; the road that loops around it is several kilometres long, and the monuments are
        spread far apart. Walking between them in the Rajasthan sun is tiring, which is why most visitors hire a taxi for
        a half-day fort tour.
    </p>
    <p>With <a href="./">Chittorgarh Taxi Services</a> you get:</p>
    <ul>
        <li>Pickup from your hotel, railway station or bus stand.</li>
        <li>A driver who knows the best order to visit the monuments and where to park.</li>
        <li>Waiting time at every stop, so you can explore at your own pace.</li>
        <li>An option to extend the trip to <a href="Sanwariya-Seth-Temple-Taxi-from-Chittorgarh.aspx">Sanwariya Seth Temple</a> or other <a href="Places-to-Visit-in-Chittorgarh.aspx">places to visit around Chittorgarh</a>.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="tips">Travel Tips for Visiting Chittorgarh Fort</h2>
    <ul>
        <li><strong>Best season:</strong> October to March, when days are pleasant. Monsoon (July&ndash;September) turns the hills green.</li>
        <li><strong>Start early:</strong> Reach by 9:30 AM to beat the heat and the crowds.</li>
        <li><strong>Wear comfortable shoes:</strong> There are steps and uneven paths, especially at Gaumukh Kund and Vijay Stambh.</li>
        <li><strong>Carry water and a cap:</strong> There is little shade between monuments.</li>
        <li><strong>Stay for sunset:</strong> The views from the western ramparts are stunning, and you can catch the light and sound show afterwards.</li>
        <li><strong>Hire a guide:</strong> Government-approved guides at the fort bring the stories of the sieges to life.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
        A visit to Chittorgarh Fort is a journey through 1,300 years of history. Book a comfortable taxi, take your time and
        let the stories of Rajput courage unfold around you.
    </p>

